    <h2>The honest math</h2>
    <p>For a five-to-fifteen-page service-business site that needs to rank locally and convert on mobile, the traditional-agency model is structurally over-priced and under-performing on the metrics that actually matter. The agency model is built for bigger projects supported by bigger teams, and a service-business website is not that kind of project. <strong>Custom-coded work paired with direct, accountable support is the right shape for it, at roughly half the five-year cost and considerably higher PageSpeed.</strong></p>
